<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ramiro II of León</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 898–951</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ramiro II was king of León from 931 to 951. In 939 he defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abd-al-rahman-iii">Abd al-Rahman III</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-simancas">Battle of Simancas</a>, one of the greatest Christian victories of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reconquista">Reconquista</a>, and pushed the frontier south to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tormes">Tormes</a>. He also contended with the ambitions of Fernán González, count of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a>, who gradually made his county independent.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ramiro-ii-of-leon.jpg" alt="Ramiro II of León" width="320" height="457" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ramiro2Leon.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Abd al-Rahman III led summer campaigns in person, but in 939 he suffered a heavy defeat by <b>Ramiro II of León</b> at the Battle of Simancas, after which he rarely took the field himself.</blockquote><a href="/empire/caliphate-of-cordoba">Caliphate of Córdoba · Military</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Ramiro II</b> (r. 931–951), allied with the count of Castile, Fernán González, defeated the caliph at the Battle of Simancas in 939, one of the few great Christian victories of the period, and resettled the Tormes valley around Salamanca.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-leon">Kingdom of León · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>The troops of King <b>Ramiro II of León</b> met those of the Cordovan caliph Abd al-Rahman III near the walls of Simancas, and Ramiro defeated the caliph's army.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/july-19">19 July in history</a></li><li><blockquote>Around 943 <b>Ramiro II of León</b> created the County of Monzón, around Monzón de Campos near Palencia, for Assur Fernández, a rival of Fernán González of Castile.</blockquote><a href="/state/county-of-monzon">County of Monzón</a></li></ul></section>
